================================================================================
1. SCHEMA REGISTRY API
================================================================================

Get list of schemas:          GET http://localhost:8081/subjects
Get schema by ID:             GET http://localhost:8081/schemas/ids/{id}
Get all versions of a schema: GET http://localhost:8081/subjects/{subject-name}/versions
Get specific version:         GET http://localhost:8081/subjects/{subject-name}/versions/{version}
Get latest version:           GET http://localhost:8081/subjects/{subject-name}/versions/latest
Register a new schema:        POST http://localhost:8081/subjects/{subject-name}/versions
    {
        "schema": "{\"type\":\"record\",\"name\":\"employee\",\"fields\":[{\"name\":\"emp_id\",\"type\":\"int\"},{\"name\":\"emp_name\",\"type\":\"string\"},{\"name\":\"dept_id\",\"type\":\"int\"}]}"
    }

Delete a specific version:    DELETE http://localhost:8081/subjects/{subject-name}/versions/{version}
Delete all versions:          DELETE http://localhost:8081/subjects/{subject-name}
Permanent delete (hard):      DELETE http://localhost:8081/subjects/{subject-name}?permanent=true

================================================================================
2. KAFKA CONNECT API
================================================================================

CLUSTER INFORMATION:
    GET http://localhost:8083/                  - Connect version info
    GET http://localhost:8083/connectors        - List all connectors
    GET http://localhost:8083/connector-plugins - List available connector plugins

CONNECTOR MANAGEMENT:

    Create Connector: POST http://localhost:8083/connectors
        {
            "name": "pg-employee-source-connector",
            "config": {
                "connector.class": "io.confluent.connect.jdbc.JdbcSourceConnector",
                "connection.url": "jdbc:postgresql://localhost:5432/srivatsan",
                "connection.user": "srivatsan",
                "connection.password": "password",
                "mode": "incrementing",
                "incrementing.column.mapping": "public.employee:emp_id",
                "topic.prefix": "pg-",
                "table.include.list": "public.employee"
            }
        }

    Get Connector:        GET http://localhost:8083/connectors/pg-employee-source-connector
    Get Connector Config: GET http://localhost:8083/connectors/pg-employee-source-connector/config
    Get Connector Status: GET http://localhost:8083/connectors/pg-employee-source-connector/status

    Update Connector: PUT http://localhost:8083/connectors/pg-employee-source-connector/config
        {
            "connector.class": "io.confluent.connect.jdbc.JdbcSourceConnector",
            "connection.url": "jdbc:postgresql://localhost:5432/srivatsan",
            "connection.user": "srivatsan",
            "connection.password": "password",
            "mode": "incrementing",
            "incrementing.column.mapping": "public.employee:emp_id",
            "topic.prefix": "pg-",
            "table.include.list": "public.employee"
        }

    Delete Connector: DELETE http://localhost:8083/connectors/pg-employee-source-connector

================================================================================
3. HANDS-ON
================================================================================

FLOW:
    Producer → Kafka Topic → Sink Connector → DB Table → Source Connector → Another Kafka Topic

Step 1: Register schema to Kafka Schema Registry
    POST http://localhost:8081/subjects/employee-value/versions
    {
        "schema": "{\"type\":\"record\",\"name\":\"employee\",\"fields\":[{\"name\":\"emp_id\",\"type\":\"int\"},{\"name\":\"emp_name\",\"type\":\"string\"},{\"name\":\"dept_id\",\"type\":\"int\"}]}"
    }

Step 2: Create table
    CREATE TABLE employee (
        emp_id SERIAL,
        emp_name VARCHAR(50),
        dept_id INTEGER,
        created_at TIMESTAMP DEFAULT CURRENT_TIMESTAMP,
        primary key (emp_id)
    );

Step 3: Setup Kafka Sink Connector
    POST http://localhost:8083/connectors
    {
        "name": "pg-employee-sink-connector",
        "config": {
            "connector.class": "io.confluent.connect.jdbc.JdbcSinkConnector",
            "connection.url": "jdbc:postgresql://localhost:5432/postgres",
            "connection.user": "srivatsan",
            "connection.password": "password",
            "topics": "employee-sink",
            "table.name.format": "employee",
            "auto.create": "true",
            "auto.evolve": "true",
            "insert.mode": "upsert",
            "pk.mode": "record_value",
            "pk.fields": "emp_id",
            "batch.size": "1000"
        }
    }

Step 4: Kafka Avro Producer
    Get the schema ID from the schema-registry and then use it in the Avro producer
    kafka-avro-console-producer --bootstrap-server localhost:9092 \
        --topic employee-sink \
        --property schema.registry.url=http://localhost:8081 \
        --property value.schema.id=1

    Sample data:
        {"emp_id": 1, "emp_name": "sriv", "dept_id": 10}
        {"emp_id": 2, "emp_name": "john", "dept_id": 20}

Step 5: Setup Source Connector
    POST http://localhost:8083/connectors
    {
        "name": "pg-employee-source-connector",
        "config": {
            "connector.class": "io.confluent.connect.jdbc.JdbcSourceConnector",
            "connection.url": "jdbc:postgresql://localhost:5432/postgres",
            "connection.user": "srivatsan",
            "connection.password": "password",
            "mode": "incrementing",
            "incrementing.column.mapping": "public.employee:emp_id",
            "topic.prefix": "pg-",
            "table.include.list": "public.employee"
        }
    }

